From: alarm-diting <alarm@diting>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Separate the TX
 SoundWire ports of the two microphones

With codec ports 1 and 2 both on master port 1, ADC1 and ADC4 are sent
in the same bit slot and the capture is white noise (seen on a unit
with the Goodix touchscreen and the 42 02 0a panel). Map codec port 2
to master port 2 (lane 2); ADC4 is then TX macro input SWR_MIC5.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts	2026-10-26 14:53:06.970849931 +0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts	2026-10-26 14:53:21.708080181 +0300
@@ -1116,7 +1116,13 @@
 	wcd_tx: codec@0,3 {
 		compatible = "sdw20217010d00";
 		reg = <0 3>;
-		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 1 2 3>;
+		/*
+		 * AMIC1 (ADC1, codec port 1) and AMIC5 (ADC4, codec port 2) are
+		 * used together: with both codec ports on master port 1 they drive
+		 * the same bit slot (white noise). Codec port 2 goes to master
+		 * port 2 (lane 2), where ADC4 arrives as SWR_MIC5.
+		 */
+		qcom,tx-port-mapping = <1 2 3 4>;
 	};
 };
 
